  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advice on Green Hydrogen Location Mapping study Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity strengthened the quality and relevance of a study on green hydrogen location mapping in West Java. The study identifies potential locations for renewable energy resources, including wind, solar, hydro and geothermal, and develops geospatial mapping of suitable sites for green hydrogen production based on factors such as infrastructure availability, proximity to industrial centres and renewable energy potential. It also assesses technical and economic feasibility, environmental considerations and potential policy and partnership opportunities.A Dutch expert provided detailed feedback on the study&#x2019;s methodology and draft report, incorporating perspectives relevant to Dutch expertise and interests in the hydrogen sector. This input helped refine the analytical approach and significantly improved the clarity and overall quality of the final report.</narrative>
  </description>
